OPM='https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/hiring-information/merit-hiring-plan-resources/applicant-guidance-on-the-two-page-resume-limit/'
guides=[
{'slug':'federal-resume-guide','title':'How to shorten a federal résumé to two pages','description':'A practical two-page federal résumé guide with a relevant-experience checklist, a supported before-and-after example and official OPM sources.','intro':'A shorter résumé should make your relevant experience easier to assess. It should not hide required employment details or turn supporting work into leadership. Start with the actual announcement, then decide which verified examples deserve the space.','sections':[
('Start with the vacancy, not the font size','Read Qualifications, Specialized Experience, How You Will Be Evaluated and Required Documents. Write down the work the agency needs evidence of. Match each requirement to something you actually did. An employer cannot assess an experience you have not described, but repeating a requirement does not prove that you meet it.'),
('Make a relevance map','For each important duty, list the task you performed, the tool or process you used, and your own contribution. Keep an outcome only when you can substantiate it. If you supported a coordinator, say supported or assisted. Do not convert the announcement’s desired qualifications into your qualifications.'),
('Keep the employment facts visible','For relevant employment, keep employer, job title, month/year dates and hours per week. Include your actual federal series and grade for federal positions. Your target grade is not your previously held grade. Include current contact information and the education or credentials relevant to the announcement. Follow its specific instructions.'),
('Cut repetition before cutting meaning','Replace repeated descriptions with distinct evidence. Group related actions when doing so remains readable. Reduce generic objectives, long lists of personality traits and unrelated detail. Prioritize the examples that demonstrate the required level of work. A two-page maximum is not a requirement to fill two pages.'),
('Check the exported file','Review the final PDF page by page. Keep headings with their text, use readable type, and check dates, hours and contact details. Reopen the Word file if you intend to edit it. Editing can change pagination, so inspect the final version you actually submit. The announcement controls required documents and any applicable exception.')],
'rough':'Helped with reports and training. Worked with records.',
'facts':'Prepared weekly Excel reports for the coordinator. Assisted with training schedules for 12 staff by checking availability and tracking attendance.',
'after':'Prepared weekly operational reports in Excel for the coordinator. Assisted with training schedules for 12 staff, checking availability and tracking attendance.',
'note':'The staff count comes from the fictional source facts. This example does not claim the applicant supervised the staff or improved performance by an invented percentage.','target':'federal'},
{'slug':'military-to-civilian-resume','title':'Translate military experience into a civilian résumé','description':'Translate military duties into clear civilian language while preserving your actual authority, tools, qualifications and accomplishments.','intro':'A civilian hiring manager may not recognize a military billet or acronym. Explain the work in language the employer understands, while keeping your official service history and responsibilities accurate. Translation is about clarity, not upgrading your authority.','sections':[
('Choose one target role','A résumé for logistics coordination needs different examples from one for training or customer support. Read the target duties first. Identify the actions and tools you already know, then choose relevant service examples. Do not add commercial software or industry experience merely because it appears in the posting.'),
('Keep the official role accurate','Retain your real service branch, title and dates. You may add a plain-language explanation alongside a title when it accurately describes the work. Do not replace your official title with an invented civilian title or describe military service as federal civilian employment.'),
('Explain the task and your part','Ask: what did I organize, inspect, maintain, document or teach? Who used my work? Which equipment or procedures did I actually use? Distinguish performing, assisting, supervising and commanding. If an outcome was a team result, describe your contribution rather than claiming it all.'),
('Use numbers you can support','Personnel counts, inventory quantities and training sessions can provide useful scope when they are accurate and appropriate to disclose. A strong bullet does not need a percentage. Leave unsupported savings, readiness increases and performance claims out.'),
('Keep sensitive details out','Use only information appropriate for a public job application. Do not paste classified, operationally sensitive or unnecessary personal information into a résumé tool. For credentials and clearances, include only accurate information that is appropriate and relevant to the vacancy. Never imply a license transfers automatically.'),
('Check the hiring path separately','Veterans’ preference and hiring authorities are separate from résumé writing. Eligibility depends on your circumstances and the vacancy. Read the announcement and official agency instructions; a résumé tool cannot determine eligibility or guarantee referral.')],
'rough':'Helped train new people and maintained equipment logs.',
'facts':'Demonstrated the equipment inspection checklist to new team members. Recorded inspection results and reported missing items to the team leader.',
'after':'Demonstrated equipment inspection procedures to new team members. Maintained inspection records and reported missing items to the team leader.',
'note':'This example does not invent an instructor certification, supervisory role, equipment qualification or readiness result.','target':'private'},
{'slug':'resume-employment-gaps','title':'How to explain an employment gap on your résumé','description':'Handle an employment gap honestly, choose relevant transferable experience and describe a return to work without inventing employment.','intro':'An employment gap does not require a fabricated job or an overly personal explanation. Keep dates accurate, focus on the role you want now, and include activities only when they actually occurred and help explain relevant experience.','sections':[
('Keep dates accurate','Do not extend an end date to cover a break or label a period as consulting when you did no consulting work. Use a consistent month/year format. For federal applications, follow the announcement’s employment-information requirements rather than using a format that conceals dates.'),
('Choose whether a short explanation helps','A brief career-break entry can clarify an otherwise confusing timeline, but it is not always necessary. If you include one, use truthful wording you are comfortable sharing. You do not need to provide a diagnosis or unnecessary family details. Never let a writing tool invent the reason for a break.'),
('Use real activities, not filler','Relevant coursework, projects, volunteering or freelance work may belong on the résumé if you actually completed them. Label each activity correctly. Do not turn an unfinished course into a degree, a personal project into paid employment, or informal help into a licensed professional role.'),
('Lead with current relevant strengths','Choose recent experience that connects to the vacancy. Describe the tools, records, customers or processes you worked with. If you are changing careers, explain transferable experience without claiming you already held the target job.'),
('Prepare a concise interview explanation','A simple explanation can state that you took time away, identify relevant activity if there was any, and return the discussion to the work you can do now. Do not claim a completed qualification, unrestricted availability or a resolved issue unless that is true for you.'),
('Review the whole timeline','Compare the résumé with your application form and any required employment history. Check that dates and job titles agree. A concise résumé can prioritize relevant jobs while an application form may separately ask for a complete history.')],
'rough':'I worked retail before taking a break. I want an office job.',
'facts':'Store Associate, Example Retail, July 2019–December 2020. Updated an Excel stock-count worksheet and answered customer questions. Career break, January 2021–June 2022; no employment during that period is claimed.',
'after':'Updated an Excel stock-count worksheet and answered customer questions using approved product information. Career break: January 2021–June 2022.',
'note':'The example keeps the break visible and does not invent office employment, training or a reason for the time away.','target':'career-change'},
{'slug':'federal-police-resume','title':'Federal police résumé examples: training and supervisory work','description':'Describe verified police training, watch operations and supervisory experience clearly for a federal vacancy without overstating your responsibilities.','intro':'Police experience can include enforcement, documentation, training and watch operations. A useful federal résumé connects your own work to the vacancy’s specialized experience. The series or grade you want is not evidence that you have already performed at that level.','sections':[
('Separate the role you held from the role you want','Use your actual employer, title, federal series and grade when applicable. Keep month/year dates and hours per week for relevant employment. Describe acting assignments accurately; do not turn occasional coverage into a permanent promotion.'),
('Show what training involved','State whether you demonstrated a procedure, coached a trainee, evaluated performance or coordinated a program. Mention the actual records, checklists or standards you used when appropriate to disclose. Use verified trainee counts or session numbers only when available. Do not invent an instructor credential.'),
('Describe supervisory authority precisely','Distinguish passing information, assigning work, reviewing reports, approving leave, evaluating staff and making disciplinary recommendations. Include only responsibilities you actually held. The word supervised should reflect real authority, not simply being the most experienced officer present.'),
('Connect operational examples to the vacancy','An announcement may emphasize patrol, physical security, investigations, training or administrative review. Select supporting examples from your background. Explain the action and contribution in plain language without listing every tool or acronym you have encountered.'),
('Protect case and operational information','Use appropriate general descriptions. Exclude victim identifiers, restricted procedures, sensitive facility information and unnecessary case detail. A résumé is not an incident report, and a writing tool should not receive protected operational records.'),
('Review required documentation','Read the vacancy’s qualification, assessment and required-document instructions. Add licenses, training, education or other qualifications only when held and relevant. Neither a résumé example nor matching keywords establishes eligibility or guarantees referral.')],
'rough':'Helped new officers learn the desk and checked paperwork.',
'facts':'Demonstrated desk-journal procedures to newly assigned officers. Checked completed journal entries for missing times and returned them to the officer for correction. No formal supervisory appointment is claimed.',
'after':'Demonstrated desk-journal procedures to newly assigned officers. Reviewed entries for missing times and returned incomplete entries for correction.',
'note':'This fictional example shows training and review work without inventing supervisory authority, certifications or a measurable error reduction.','target':'federal'}]
brand='<a class="logo" href="/">CareerLaunch<span>AI</span></a>'
def shell(slug,title,description,body,article=True):
    canonical='https://resumebuilder.shop/'+slug
    return f'''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>{e(title)} | CareerLaunch AI</title><meta name="description" content="{e(description)}"><link rel="canonical" href="{canonical}"><meta property="og:type" content="{'article' if article else 'website'}"><meta property="og:title" content="{e(title)}"><meta property="og:description" content="{e(description)}"><meta property="og:url" content="{canonical}"><meta property="og:image" content="https://resumebuilder.shop/media/careerlaunch-share.png"><link rel="icon" href="/mark.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/growth.css"><script src="/growth.js" defer></script></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-header">{brand}</header><main id="main" class="shell growth-main">{body}</main><footer><div class="footer-top">{brand}<p>Your experience. Clearly expressed.</p></div><div class="footer-links"><a href="/guides">Résumé guides</a><a href="/examples">Examples & videos</a><a href="/contact">Contact & support</a><a href="/privacy.html">Privacy</a><a href="/terms.html">Terms</a><a href="/policies">Revisions & refunds</a></div><p class="fine">Independent service. No affiliation with USAJOBS, OPM or any government agency. No guarantee of referral, interviews or employment.</p></footer></body></html>'''
def cta(target):
    return f'''<aside class="growth-cta"><h2>Start with your own experience.</h2><p>Build an outline and save your details with a free account. Pro AI writing starts at $12.99/month. The $4.99 seven-day plan includes manual editing and exports, not AI writing.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" data-growth-event="builder_cta" href="/start?type={target}">Build my résumé outline</a><a class="text-link" href="/#pricing">Compare plans</a></div><p class="fine">Your outline is not an AI-written résumé. Review every generated claim and your final documents before applying.</p></aside>'''
for g in guides:
    body=f'<nav class="growth-crumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/guides">Résumé guides</a> / Practical guide</nav><p class="eyebrow">YOUR FACTS. A CLEARER APPLICATION.</p><h1>{e(g["title"])}</h1><p class="lead">{e(g["intro"])}</p><p class="fine">CareerLaunch AI editorial team · Reviewed October 29, 2026 · Informational guidance</p><div class="growth-article">'
    for i,(title,paragraph) in enumerate(g['sections'],1): body+=f'<section><h2>{i}. {e(title)}</h2><p>{e(paragraph)}</p></section>'
    body+=f'<section class="growth-example"><p class="eyebrow">FICTIONAL WORKED EXAMPLE</p><h2>Improve the wording. Keep the facts.</h2><h3>Rough description</h3><p>{e(g["rough"])}</p><h3>Verified facts supplied for this example</h3><p>{e(g["facts"])}</p><h3>Clearer wording</h3><blockquote>{e(g["after"])}</blockquote><p class="fine">{e(g["note"])}</p></section>'
    if g['target']=='federal': body+=f'<section><h2>Check the official requirements</h2><p>OPM’s current guidance sets the two-page framework and identifies relevant employment and education details. Read the exact announcement before submitting.</p><a class="text-link" href="{OPM}">Read OPM’s applicant guidance</a></section>'
    body+='</div>'+cta(g['target'])+'<section><h2>Keep building your application</h2><div class="growth-grid">'
    for other in guides:
        if other!=g: body+=f'<a class="growth-card" href="/{other["slug"]}">{e(other["title"])}</a>'
    body+='</div><p><a class="text-link" href="/examples">Watch the fictional examples →</a></p></section>'
    (ROOT/(g['slug']+'.html')).write_text(shell(g['slug'],g['title'],g['description'],body))
